    "q-97009": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97009",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that $A=PD{P}^{-1},$ which of the following could be matrices $D$ and $P?$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $A=PD{P}^{-1}$ is a diagonalization of the matrix $A.$ So let's apply the diagonalization algorithm to $A.$\n\n**Step 1.** We need to find the eigenvalues of $A.$ Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, the eigenvalues are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=-2\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=1.$\n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$\n\n- Consider $\\lambda =-2.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-2)I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which is already in row echelon:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $3$rd). This implies that we will have $3-2=1$ linearly independent eigenvector corresponding to the current eigenvalue. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{-2})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ is *not* diagonalizable, since \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{1})+\\text{dim}({V}_{-2})=1+1=2\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-97009-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$A$ is not diagonalizable",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"71\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is not diagonalizable"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-97009-b",
              "type": "text",
